  "description": "CW34 (COW \u00a711.11): `var l0 = a.l0` / `var c1 = l0[i0]` in a read-modify-write region bind through cow_bind_rmw_handle -- a borrow when the runtime spine is unshared -- instead of the S9.1.2 snapshot bind (cow_bind_var / cow_mark_shared), and the store-backs `l0[i0] = c1` / `a.l0 = l0` carry no cow_capture_value mark: the only capture left in the body is the legitimate S9.3.1 one on `c1[i1] = val` (a named parameter value stored into a container). With the snapshot bind every call copied every level (cd/havlak arr_set: 220k/205k copies per run). S9.1.3/LR12-33 (2026-10-28): the generic plain val input may itself alias the var root, so one entry cow_mark_shared is required. Neither RMW handle binds through cow_bind_var; both still use cow_bind_rmw_handle and store-backs add no capture.",
